<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/stylesheets/style.css" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/stylesheets/partials.css" />
  <title>DOS Games Blog</title>
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('./partials/_navbar.ejs') %>

  <main>
    <% if(user){ %>
      <h1>Welcome back, <%= user.username %>!</h1>
    <% } else { %>
      <h1>Welcome to the DOS Games Blog!</h1>
    <% } %>

    <% if (user && user.role === 'admin') { %>
      <a href="/posts/new" class="btn">+ New Post</a>
    <% } %>

    <section class="dos-article">
      <h2>What Was DOS?</h2>
      <p>DOS (Disk Operating System) was a text-based, single-tasking OS where users typed commands instead of using a mouse. It ran one program at a time (system crashes were total) and introduced standard conventions like C:\ drive paths and 3-letter extensions (.exe, .txt).</p>
      <img src="/images/Ms-dosdir.png" alt="MS-DOS command line showing a directory listing" />
      <img src="/images/d4631bc8f399e21587ad219057d3e015.jpg" alt="DOS running the Norton Commander file manager" />
      <h3>Who Owned It?</h3>
      <p>Tim Paterson created 86-DOS in 4 months at Seattle Computer Products. Microsoft bought it in 1981 for $50,000, licensing it to IBM (as PC-DOS) and selling it to other vendors (as MS-DOS) to build a multi-billion-dollar business.</p>

      <h3>Timeline</h3>
      <p>DOS was the main PC OS for 14 years (1981-1995). Windows 95 took over the interface, and Microsoft retired the underlying codebase completely in 2000.</p>

      <h3>Floppy Disk Formats</h3>
      <p>DOS relied on floppy disks for boot files, software, and storage across three generations:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>8-inch (1970s): 80 KB - 1.2 MB (flexible sleeve)</li>
        <li>5.25-inch (1980s): 360 KB - 1.2 MB (flexible jacket; early IBM PC standard)</li>
        <li>3.5-inch (1990s): 1.44 MB (rigid shell with metal shutter)</li>
      </ul>
      <img src="/images/disk1.jpg" alt="Microsoft MS-DOS 6.22 install diskette" />
      <img src="/images/1235401302_589578.jpg" alt="Sony internal 3.5 inch floppy disk drive" />
    </section>

    <% if (posts && posts.length > 0) { %>
      <div class="post-list">
        <% posts.forEach(post => { %>
          <div class="post-card">
            <h2><a href="/posts/<%= post._id %>"><%= post.title %></a></h2>
            <p><%= post.body.substring(0, 50) %>...</p>
          </div>
        <% }) %>
      </div>
    <% } %>
  </main>

  <%- include('./partials/_footer.ejs') %>
</body>
</html>